  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## What's changed\n\nNative upgrade: the packages now bind\n[dd-sdk-ios 3.15.0](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-sdk-ios/releases/tag/3.15.0), up from `3.14.0`.\n\n> **Package versions are `<dd-sdk-ios version>.<binding revision>`.** `3.15.0.1` is dd-sdk-ios\n> `3.15.0`, binding revision `1`. The fourth component belongs to this repository and advances when\n> the bindings or packaging change while the native binaries stay put.\n\nThe bound Objective-C surface moved by exactly one member, so this is close to a version bump —\nbut not quite one, because that member is a new datacenter and an app on it could not have been\nconfigured before.\n\n## `DDSite.Uk1()` — the UK1 datacenter\n\nDatadog's UK1 site is now reachable:\n\n```csharp\nvar configuration = new DDConfiguration(clientToken: \"<CLIENT_TOKEN>\", env: \"production\")\n{\n    Site = DDSite.Uk1(),\n};\n```\n\n`DDSite` is a class of static factory methods, so it is `DDSite.Uk1()`, not a constant. The full\nset is now `Us1()`, `Us3()`, `Us5()`, `Eu1()`, `Ap1()`, `Ap2()`, `Uk1()`, `Us1_fed()`,\n`Us2_fed()`.\n\n## Everything else upstream changed, without changing the API\n\nNone of these needed a binding change — they are behaviour inside the native binaries the\npackages carry, so an app gets them by moving to `3.15.0.1`:\n\n- **Session Replay captures more faithfully** — visual effects, embedded content and gradients.\n- **KSCrash is bumped to 2.5.1** inside `DatadogCrashReporting`.\n- **WebView tracing no longer drops early requests.** `onSessionStart` now fires only once the\n  sampling information WebView Tracking depends on is in place.\n- **`onSessionStart` no longer crashes in Swift 6 projects** — not reachable from C#, but it is in\n  the same binary.\n- **WebView RUM `ddtags` are merged by key**, so duplicate keys stop appearing.\n\nUpstream's own notes are the reference:\n[3.14.0…3.15.0](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-sdk-ios/compare/3.14.0...3.15.0).\n\n## How the surface was checked\n\n`./build/DiffSwiftHeaders.sh` against the 3.14.0 headers reports one framework changed\n(`DatadogCore`) and one added line in it — `+ (DDSite * _Nonnull)uk1`. The other nine frameworks\nthat ship a generated Objective-C header are byte-identical in it, so their committed\n`ApiDefinitions.cs` files are still exact. `OpenTelemetryApi` is outside that comparison — it\nships no `-Swift.h` — and is unmoved anyway: 3.15.0 pins the same OpenTelemetryApi release 3.14.0\ndid.\n\n`./build/GenerateDeviceClassAliases.sh` was re-run against the 3.15.0 binaries, as the upgrade\nchecklist requires. It finds the same 41 classes, under the same Swift mangled names, so\n`build/device-class-aliases/` is unchanged and the device-link repair from 3.14.0.5 carries over\nuntouched.\n\n## Upgrading from 3.14.0.5\n\n```diff\n-<PackageReference Include=\"DatadogNet.RUM.iOS\" Version=\"3.14.0.5\" />\n+<PackageReference Include=\"DatadogNet.RUM.iOS\" Version=\"3.15.0.1\" />\n```\n\nNothing else to change. No type moved, nothing was removed or renamed, and the package set is the\nsame; all packages move together as they depend on each other at an exact version.",
